      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at [Linux kernel code](https://github.com/spotify/linux/blob/master/net/core/rtnetlink.c#L1339) RTM_NEWLINK is used together with IFF_UP \nIn my understanding, `RTM_NEWLINK` is used for updating or configuring properties of an existing network interface. This includes changing its administrative state (e.g., bringing it up or down) by setting or clearing the IFF_UP flag, while RTM_SETLINK is used to emphasize that the operation modifies an existing link rather than creating a new one",
