      "writtenOn": "2024-12-09T01:37:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes we should we this, otherwise we may modify other flags unexpectedly. Probably we can set change inside the method and, something like:\n```\n    protected static RtNetlinkLinkMessage createSetFlagsMessage(\n            @NonNull String interfaceName, int sequenceNumber, int add_flags, int remove_flags\n            @NonNull OsAccess osAccess) {\n                int change \u003d 0;\n                for (flag in add_flags) { change |\u003d flag;}\n                for (flag in remove_flags) { change |\u003d ~flag;}\n            }\n```",
      "parentUuid": "ce32dc25_6238c0e3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 343,
        "startChar": 83,
        "endLine": 343,
        "endChar": 96
